---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO } from '../links';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy: Prowl"
  description="What Prowl stores, who it talks to, and what it never does. Prowl runs in your browser and only contacts GitHub."
>
  <article class="section wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      Prowl is a browser extension that runs on your device. It has no backend and collects no
      data.
    </p>
    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your GitHub token, your settings and the last pull request data Prowl fetched are stored in
      the browser's extension storage (<code>chrome.storage.local</code>). Your token is sent only
      to GitHub, to authenticate its API requests. Settings and pull request data are not sent anywhere.
      Signing out removes your token and the fetched data; uninstalling Prowl removes everything.
    </p>
    <h2>Who Prowl talks to</h2>
    <p>
      Only GitHub: the GitHub API, with your token, to read and act on your pull requests, and
      GitHub's avatar images. There are no analytics, no telemetry, no ads and no other servers.
    </p>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The site is static. It sets no cookies, runs no scripts and loads no third-party resources.
      GitHub Pages hosts it and may keep its own server logs.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Prowl is open source. Read the code or open an issue in <a href={REPO}>the repository</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
